Name the root `invoke_agent` span for the SDK rather than for a subagent the
caller declared. `options.agents` defines, in the SDK's own words, "custom
subagents invokable via the Agent tool" — delegation targets, not the agent
being invoked — so with one declared the root took its name while the Task call
that reached it opened a nested span under the same name, and declaring a second
silently renamed the root back. Both shapes broke anything keyed on the span
name, and the package's own usage example declares exactly one agent.
